{number: 4}
{title: To God Be the Glory}
{key: G}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[G] To God be the glory, great [D] things He hath done,
So [D7] loved He the world that He [G] gave us His Son,
Who [G] yielded His life an a-[C] tonement for sin,
And [G] opened the life gate that [D] all may go [G] in.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G] Praise the Lord, praise the Lord,
Let the [D] earth hear His voice!
[D7] Praise the Lord, praise the Lord,
Let the [G] people rejoice!
O [G] come to the Father thro’ [C] Jesus the Son,
And [G] give Him the glory; great [D] things He hath [G] done.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[G] O perfect redemption, the [D] purchase of blood,
To [D7] every believer the [G] promise of God;
The [G] vilest offender who [C] truly believes,
That [G] moment from Jesus a [D] pardon re-[G] ceives.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[G] Great things He hath taught us, great [D] things He hath done,
And [D7] great our rejoicing thro’ [G] Jesus the Son;
But [G] purer, and higher, and [C] greater will be
Our [G] wonder, our transport, when [D] Jesus we [G] see.
{end_of_verse}
